<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Adrian IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1100–1159</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Nicholas Breakspear</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Adrian IV (c. 1100–1159), born Nicholas Breakspear, was the only English pope, reigning from 1154 to 1159. As papal legate to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a> in 1152–1154 he founded the archbishopric of Nidaros (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trondheim">Trondheim</a>), giving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> its own church province, and reorganised the Swedish church. As pope he crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> emperor in 1155, but relations between them soon broke down.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-adrian-iv.jpg" alt="Pope Adrian IV" width="300" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown medieval illustrator · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adrian_IV,_servus_servorum_dei_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
